From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 04:43:09 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 3219 msi: _Streams commit copies a stream from its start

msi_commit_streams wrote a stream with write_stream(), which read the source
from its current position. A just-inserted stream that had been read before
the database commit (MsiRecordReadStream on a fetched _Streams row) was left
at its end, the copy found fewer bytes than the stream size and the commit
failed with E_INVALIDARG. The source is rewound first. Gate fastmsib1 reads
s4 before the commit and checks its content after reopening; mutant
SG_MUTANT_MSIS_SEEK is caught.

diff --git a/dlls/msi/streams.c b/dlls/msi/streams.c
index 9ed2d42..23c209f 100644
--- a/dlls/msi/streams.c
+++ b/dlls/msi/streams.c
@@ -686,6 +686,11 @@ static HRESULT write_stream( IStream *dst, IStream *src )
     pos.QuadPart = 0;
     hr = IStream_Seek( dst, pos, STREAM_SEEK_SET, NULL );
     if (FAILED( hr )) return hr;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MSIS_SEEK
+    /* the source may have been read before the commit: copy it from the start */
+    hr = IStream_Seek( src, pos, STREAM_SEEK_SET, NULL );
+    if (FAILED( hr )) return hr;
+#endif
 
     for (;;)
     {
